  "question": "Background / Context\nThe project involves developing a restaurant management system for Little Lemon, a dining establishment. The system will facilitate handling restaurant operations like table bookings, order management, and menu management, integrating customer and staff information to streamline restaurant services.\n\n Objectives\n- To enable customers to book tables and place orders efficiently.\n- To manage and update menu offerings comprehensively.\n- To track order delivery status accurately.\n- To store and manage customer and staff information securely.\n\n Stakeholders & Users\n- Customers: Individuals or groups wishing to dine at the restaurant.\n- Restaurant Staff: Includes waitstaff, chefs, and managers responsible for service and operations.\n- Administrators: Personnel managing the system’s backend for data entry and updates.\n\n Functional Descriptions\n1. Bookings Management:\n   - Customers can book tables specifying the date, number of persons, and table number.\n   - Staff members are associated with each booking for service assignment.\n\n2. Order Management:\n   - Orders can be placed by staff, detailing order date, quantity, and total cost.\n   - Orders must be linked to specific bookings and include detailed order contents from the menu.\n\n3. Order Delivery Status:\n   - The system tracks the delivery status of each order, including delivery date and status updates.\n\n4. Menu Management:\n   - Supports maintaining an updated catalog of available menu items, categorized by starters, cuisines, courses, drinks, and desserts, including pricing.\n\n5. Customer and Staff Management:\n   - Stores comprehensive customer details including names and contact information.\n   - Manages staff information such as roles, salaries, and contact details, ensuring secure access.\n\n Non-Functional Descriptions\n- Scalability: The system should handle a large volume of bookings and orders seamlessly.\n- Usability: The interface needs to be intuitive for both customers and staff.\n- Security: Customer and staff data must be securely handled, with sensitive information protected.\n- Reliability: The system must ensure consistent operation without failures, especially during peak hours.",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0214\nCREATE TABLE `customers` (\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `first_name` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `last_name` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `phone_number` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`customer_id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `email` (`email`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `staff` (\n  `staff_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `first_name` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `last_name` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `role` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `salary` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `phone_number` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`staff_id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `email` (`email`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `menu_items` (\n  `menu_item_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `item_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `category` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `description` varchar(500) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `price` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `is_available` tinyint(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT '1',\n  PRIMARY KEY (`menu_item_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `bookings` (\n  `booking_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `staff_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `booking_date` date NOT NULL,\n  `booking_time` time DEFAULT NULL,\n  `number_of_persons` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `table_number` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(50) NOT NULL DEFAULT 'booked',\n  PRIMARY KEY (`booking_id`),\n  KEY `customer_id` (`customer_id`),\n  KEY `staff_id` (`staff_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `bookings_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`customer_id`) REFERENCES `customers` (`customer_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `bookings_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`staff_id`) REFERENCES `staff` (`staff_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `orders` (\n  `order_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `booking_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `staff_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `order_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `quantity` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `total_cost` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `delivery_date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `delivery_status` varchar(50) NOT NULL DEFAULT 'pending',\n  PRIMARY KEY (`order_id`),\n  KEY `booking_id` (`booking_id`),\n  KEY `staff_id` (`staff_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `orders_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`booking_id`) REFERENCES `bookings` (`booking_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `orders_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`staff_id`) REFERENCES `staff` (`staff_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `order_items` (\n  `order_item_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `order_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `menu_item_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `quantity` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `unit_price` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `line_total` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`order_item_id`),\n  KEY `order_id` (`order_id`),\n  KEY `menu_item_id` (`menu_item_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `order_items_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`order_id`) REFERENCES `orders` (`order_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `order_items_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`menu_item_id`) REFERENCES `menu_items` (`menu_item_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
